  ('Richard Pearson', 'Tregonissey A', 'Player', 7, 'playing', '{"hand":"Left","started":"11, Saturday mornings, something to do","first_memory":"Watching Steve Davis and Dennis Taylor''s black ball finish at the World Champs","highest_break":"118","achievement":"Winning nearly every league in Cornwall, and getting the highest break in the Mining League the year we won it","ambition":"Loads, but age is against me, I suppose to do well or win the county singles","memorable_match":"Far to many to name","favourite_pro":"Ronnie O''Sulllivan, pure genius","commentator":"Stephen Hendry and Ken Doherty","famous_met":"Ronnie O''Sullivan, Jimmy White, Steve Davis, Stephen Hendry, Paul Hunter, Matthew Stephens, basically most of them, I have been lucky to have played a lot of them as well","bogey":"Don''t really have one","best_player":"Currently - probably Andrew Best, but in the past Barrie McIntosh","underrated":"Me!","funniest":"Lights went out in match, iron was put down, lights back on, carried on ironing the table to find out the floor on which the iron was on was full of dirt, ironed the cloth and melted the cloth"}'::jsonb, null),
